    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessService" name="Investment Portfolio Planning" id="id-3ac884e0561240318a67e7e89fb20182">
      <documentation>** 1. Role ** 
Agree the customer investment portfolio governing principles, risk appetite, management/trading guidelines and target portfolio profile. Identify any desired/target and 'out of bounds' securities/sectors. Ensure disclosures and related eligibility, suitability and other regulatory obligations are addressed and reflected in the agreement 

 

** 2. Examples of use ** 

A relationship manager established the investment agreement for a customer that is setting up a managed investment portfolio 

 

** 3.Executive Summary ** 

Agree the policies and required make-up of an investment portfolio and ensure all required bank and regulatory terms and conditions are addressed 

 

** 4. Key Features ** 

Identify and agree investment portfolio properties and make-up (includes risk appetite) 

Handle regulatory and bank requirements (e.g. disclosures, suitability, eligibility) 

Identify any target and securities to avoid 

Agree key roles and schedules for the investment portfolio handling 

https://bian.org/servicelandscape-13-0-0/object_22.html?object=40803
</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessService" name="Investment Portfolio Analysis" id="id-f59004a91db8422293cf0a2fd6828f4c">
      <documentation>** 1. Role ** 
Perform scheduled and ad-hoc performance analysis on a customer's investment portfolio. This can include different types of analysis and performance comparisons 

 

** 2. Examples of use ** 

A relationship manager requests an investment portfolio performance analysis prior to a regular client meeting 

 

** 3.Executive Summary ** 

Assess and report on investment portfolio make-up, valuation and performance 

 

** 4. Key Features ** 

Consolidate investment portfolio transaction details and comparative market activity reports 

Select types of performance analysis and apply analyses to the period of transaction data 

Develop portfolio performance comparisons and evaluations/justifications 

https://bian.org/servicelandscape-13-0-0/object_22.html?object=43968</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessService" name="eTrading Workbench" id="id-f38b8589534c4c938b47e85311e1f1a9">
      <documentation>** 1. Role ** 
Operate the consumer e-trading facility (combines consumer device based application and network connectivity to the bank). This enables a customer to trade securities on their own account through the bank. A customer can initiate the execution of securities trades against their trading facility. The facility will determine and apply service/facility fees and charges as appropriate. 

 

** 2. Examples of use ** 

A consumer customer logs on to the E-branch web portal to access their e-trading account, tracks prices and research relating to his portfolio and executes and sale/purchase pair of transactions. 

 

** 3.Executive Summary ** 

This Service Domain supports consumer securities trading of their investment portfolio through the bank 

 

** 4. Key Features ** 

Investment portfolio management 

Securities valuation 

Investment opportunity identification 

Market order execution 

https://bian.org/servicelandscape-13-0-0/object_23.html?object=49273
</documentation>
